'''Randy Oglesby''' {{born|31|August|1948}}, also credited as '''Thomas Oglesby''', is an actor who has portrayed seven different ''[[Star Trek]]'' characters, most notably [[Degra]] on {{s|ENT}}. He is one of only six actors to do so, the others being [[Jeffrey Combs]], [[J.G. Hertzler]], [[Vaughn Armstrong]], [[Brent Spiner]] and [[Thomas Kopache]].

Oglesby has also guest-starred in numerous other television series, including {{wt|L.A. Law}}, ''[[The X-Files]]'', and {{wt|ER (TV series)|ER}} (2001, starring [[Eriq La Salle]], with [[Ming-Na Wen]], [[James Cromwell]], [[James Sie]] and [[Marcelo Tubert]]). He also appeared in {{wt|Angel (1999 TV series)|Angel}}, {{wt|Cold Case}}, and {{wt|JAG (TV series)|JAG}} (2002 and 2005). He has also starred {{wt|Boston Legal}} (starring [[William Shatner]], [[René Auberjonois]], and [[John Larroquette]]) and had a recurring role in {{wt|Vanished (TV series)|Vanished}}. In 2007, he appeared in {{wt|General Hospital}}, before earning another recurring role on {{wt|Dirt (TV series)|Dirt}}. He later appeared in {{wt|True Blood}} (2008, with [[John Billingsley]], [[James Parks]] and [[Graham Shiels]]), ''Lie to Me'', {{wt|Bones (TV series)|Bones}}, and {{wt|NCIS (TV series)|NCIS}}.

Oglesby has also had some film roles, most notably as Mike Dodge in {{wt|Independence Day (1996 film)|Independence Day}} (1996) and as Detective Bryson in {{wt|Liar Liar}} (1997). Other roles include a strategic analyst in {{wt|Pearl Harbor (film)|Pearl Harbor}} (2001), Lieutenant Colonel List in {{wt|We Were Soldiers}} (2002), and a harvest surgeon in ''The Island'' (2005), alongside [[Ethan Phillips]] and [[Michael Clarke Duncan]].

