'''Harry Joseph Judge''' {{born|6|July|1977}} is a Canadian actor who played four different [[Tellarite]] characters in the [[DIS Season 1|first]] and [[DIS Season 2|second season]]s of {{s|DIS}} and an episode of {{s|ST}}.

Judge played supporting roles in {{wt|Intern Academy}} (2004, with [[Matt Frewer]] and [[Saul Rubinek]]), {{wt|Identity Theft (film)|Identity Theft}} (2004), and the drama ''The Truth Below'' (2011).

Between 2013 and 2014, Judge portrayed Henry V at the Chicago Shakespeare Theater's Courtyard Theater, directed by Christopher Luscombe. {{el|www.broadwayworld.com/chicago/article/Harry-Judge-to-Lead-Chicago-Shakespeare-Theaters-HENRY-V-Cast-Announced-20140325}} {{el|showbizchicago.com/2014/05/20/the-magnificent-harry-judge-makes-henry-v-a-relatable-ruler}}

He guest-starred in episodes of ''Murdoch Mysteries'' (2011), {{wt|Nikita (TV series)|Nikita}} (2013, starring [[Aaron Stanford]], with [[Melinda Clarke]]), {{wt|Reign (TV series)|Reign}} (2014, starring [[Adelaide Kane]], with [[Nicole de Boer]]), {{wt|Saving Hope}} (2015, with [[Milton Barnes]]), {{wt|Mayday (Canadian TV series)|Mayday}} (2015), and {{wt|Lost Girl}} (2015, with [[Christopher Russell]]) followed by the drama ''Manhattan Undying'' (2016, with Milton Barnes), the short drama ''The Fall'' (2016), voice work in the video game ''Shuyan Saga'' (2017), and the television drama ''Flint'' (2017, music by [[John Debney]]).

He later appeared in episodes of ''Murdoch Mysteries'' (2018) and ''Suits'' (2018, with [[John Pyper-Ferguson]] and [[Bruce McGill]] and cinematography by [[Colin Hoult]]). He wrapped production on the stage play "Chariots of Fire" for which he performed at the Grand Theater in London, Ontario. {{instagram|p/BiZk2F3Fi_3/}} Judge appeared at the StarQuest Convention in Frederick, Maryland in July 2018 alongside [[Conrad Coates]] and [[Bill Blair]]. {{el|www.starquestconvention.com/celebrity-guests.html}}

